=== meta ===
rule: EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED
issue: 419
title: A genuinely unreadable production file still grants the opaque exemption to a rewritten expected value
origin: FP guard — the 2026-08-11 widening must not turn every unreadable prod change into a block
origin2: Kept under this name by the #419 ruling (issuecomment-6170353038: Q6 (a), rule 2) for the
origin3: expectation family, which keeps opaque-change evidence (Q1 (b)); the weakened assertion it
origin4: pinned until then moved, same inputs, to runner_opaque_native_pos. The Rust edit adds the tax
origin5: and the expected value follows it: the honest shape this guard exists for.
=== before: src/core.rs ===
pub fn invoice_total(items: &[f64], tax: f64) -> f64 {
    items.iter().sum::<f64>()
}
=== after: src/core.rs ===
pub fn invoice_total(items: &[f64], tax: f64) -> f64 {
    items.iter().sum::<f64>() * (1.0 + tax)
}
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 100.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 105.0
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED", "severity": "warn", "deescalators": ["REPAIR_EVIDENCE"]}]
